==Strategy==
This stage is straightforward with a lot of brute force on the frontline, meaning you should simply put your focus to that, as there are few working strategies. The problem lies in getting past the Metals, which can prevent most units from hitting Winged Pigge, whose rapid Omni Strikes will destroy everything in her range, including any anti-Metals brought to neutralize them.

A good unit to use here is, (unsurprisingly), [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]. Along with as many [[Cat Combo]]s as you need to properly defend him. Use [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] cats for the Owlbrows and a [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critter]] with good enough range for the [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal Enemies]], if possible (e.g., [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]]), as the Metal Hippoes can obstruct Winged Pigge from your attackers. Alternatively, you can lure and defeat the first Winged Pigge before the second spawns with Metal One Horn, such as your Critical Hitters shouldn't be troubled as much. The Angelic Gories are usually dealt with easily by whatever you brought to neutralize Winged Pigge.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - Having Resistance to Angels, Ramen is often the go-to meatshield when Winged Pigge is present, and can withstand a few hits, providing a good layer of defense even without Research Combos as long as the other threats are dealt with.
*[[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] - An Anti-Metal with a 1-second slow, 8% critical chance and single-target LD attacks, Curry's main advantage here is its ability to outrange Winged Pigge, hitting up to 475 and catching the Metals even if she gets in the way. Despite the low chance, it should not be discounted, as all that's needed are a few crits to kill the Metal Hippoes and Metal One Horn, after which the remaining units can safely take down Winged Pigge.
*[[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]] - With [[Massive Damage]] against Floating and Angel with [[Long Distance]] piercing, they ensure you will have no problem in taking down Winged Pigge. They can also kill off the Owlbrows for a nice cash injection every minute or so. Keep in mind their fragility, as two hits from Winged Pigge (one in 2/{{3c}}) are enough to knock them out.

==='''Strategy 1 (Cheese)'''===
This cheese requires luck for [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]] to kill the Metal Hippoes, so resetting may be required.

Bring a Money Start Up (M) combo (eg. [[Bento Special (Combo)|Bento Special]] or [[Offshore Accounts (Combo)|Rich Cat III's Combo]]), along with a Cat Cannon Start up (M) combo (eg. [[Yesterday's Enemy (Combo)|Yesterday's Enemy]]). Equip the Breakerblast cannon.

As soon as you can afford it, send out Catyphoon. Afterwards, start spamming [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]]. With some luck, Catyphoon will kill all 3 Metal Hippoes and max out your wallet.

Start sending out small rushers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]. When the first Owlbrow spawns, immediately send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. After the third Owlbrow spawns, which should be relatively quick, use the Breakerblast Cannon to knock them behind the base. This should let Manic Mohawk protect your other units and rush down the base safely.

==Trivia==
*The name of this stage is a reference to the former safeguard practice of taking live canaries into [[The Gelatin Mines|coal mines]]. If gaseous toxins like methane or carbon monoxide were present in the mineshaft, the canary's rapid breathing rate would cause it to perish early, effectively working as a rudimentary "gas-powered alarm" and giving the miners enough time to safely withdraw.

